  "note": "Extracted by hand from the ordering schematic. One series, MS3000X, with the metal seated standards fixed by the sheet itself: chrome carbide coated ball and seats with 17-4 PH stem as the only listed trim, Marwear Class V the only listed seat, graphite the only listed packing, each with a non-standard escape. Sizes marked with the sheet's own asterisk, 1/4, 3/8, 1-1/4 and 3 x 2 inch, are consult factory and carried as cautions. The operation table runs P2 to PB and S1 to S9 with electrics from M2 to MC and no P1, SA or SJ, exactly as printed. The positioner R label prints DA where the pattern says SR; transcribed as printed, the pairing rule is not asserted for R, and the suspected misprint is held for Marwin. Nema 7 electric remains a caution per James, July 2026. Siemens is named per the CV3000 decision.",
